  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "Suppose $f:\\mathbb R\\to\\mathbb R$ is a strictly increasing function. Show that $f$ is injective.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f$ is injective.\n\nDistinct inputs have distinct outputs because $f$ is strictly increasing.",
      "worked": "Let $x,y\\in\\mathbb R$ with $x\\ne y$.\n\nIf $x<y$, strict increase gives $f(x)<f(y)$, so $f(x)\\ne f(y)$.\n\nIf $x>y$, strict increase gives $f(x)>f(y)$, so $f(x)\\ne f(y)$.\n\nThus distinct inputs have distinct outputs, so $f$ is injective.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
